WEBVTT

00:05.230 --> 00:09.140
Your Highness! Your Highness, 
where are you going?

00:09.140 --> 00:11.870
It is past time for your 
afternoon lessons to begin.

00:13.580 --> 00:15.200
Your Highness!

00:19.770 --> 00:22.870
You walk too quickly, Your Highness.

00:24.460 --> 00:27.400
Didn't I tell you I hate 
being called "Your Highness"?

00:27.400 --> 00:28.840
My name is Clarke!

00:28.840 --> 00:30.510
Nevertheless, Your Highness...

00:30.510 --> 00:31.940
I won't answer to that anymore.

00:32.410 --> 00:35.220
My goodness, you certainly are stubborn...

00:35.510 --> 00:37.250
Prince Clarke.

00:38.480 --> 00:41.100
Well then, let us return to your room.

00:41.560 --> 00:42.590
Don't wanna!

00:42.590 --> 00:44.110
Wait, Your High—

00:44.110 --> 00:47.950
Prince Clarke! Prince Clarke!

00:47.950 --> 00:50.340
You still have your lessons!

00:50.340 --> 00:53.080
Sebastian can never keep up with me.

01:14.880 --> 01:16.200
Leticia.

01:34.390 --> 01:35.480
Um...

02:08.620 --> 02:13.530
Is it really okay for me to pursue you?

04:07.020 --> 04:07.890
Oh?

04:09.830 --> 04:11.370
You win.

04:12.140 --> 04:13.860
One more round, Nathan!

04:13.860 --> 04:16.260
Hey, go easy on me.

04:16.260 --> 04:17.610
How old do you think I am?

04:19.190 --> 04:21.370
Thirty... two!

04:21.370 --> 04:23.910
Ah! H-Hey! Wait!

04:25.550 --> 04:27.370
Father. Mother.

04:27.640 --> 04:29.900
What is it, Clarke?

04:29.900 --> 04:34.720
You've never asked to speak to us 
like this before, have you?

04:34.720 --> 04:37.130
I've found something that I want.

04:43.970 --> 04:46.020
Did you get a look at my favorite steed?

04:47.610 --> 04:48.820
Yeah.

04:48.820 --> 04:50.560
It's a beautiful, strong horse.

04:50.560 --> 04:54.570
It runs and jumps well for me,
and it does wonderfully over obstacles.

04:55.580 --> 04:58.650
I'm planning to take a long ride 
tomorrow. What do you say?

04:58.650 --> 04:59.720
Sounds great!

04:59.720 --> 05:03.160
My, what a fabulous 
conservatory you have here.

05:07.580 --> 05:12.000
Crystal, indeed! 
Everything about it is beautiful.

05:12.000 --> 05:13.820
Just like me.

05:15.160 --> 05:16.710
Uncle.

05:16.710 --> 05:19.470
Do not address me that way.
 You will call me Neil.

05:19.470 --> 05:21.200
Sure thing, Uncle Neil.

05:21.200 --> 05:22.590
Watch it, nephew!

05:23.210 --> 05:24.140
Hmph!

05:24.470 --> 05:29.730
By the way, it would seem there's an unused 
bath in the back corner. What is that?

05:30.040 --> 05:32.190
I hear it was a hot spring,

05:32.190 --> 05:35.300
but it was filled in when 
we lost our maintenance person.

05:35.300 --> 05:37.220
It appears to be a Roman bath.

05:37.220 --> 05:39.790
A Roman bath? Do those things still exist?

05:39.790 --> 05:41.820
Did yours dry up?

05:41.820 --> 05:43.240
Not entirely.

05:43.240 --> 05:47.390
What a waste! It would make such 
a lovely place for couples to chat.

05:47.390 --> 05:49.430
Hey, that would be great!

05:49.430 --> 05:51.750
I wonder if Lettie would like that.

05:51.750 --> 05:56.240
Oh, I'm sure she would. In fact, 
I know people capable of restoring it.

05:56.240 --> 05:57.510
I'd be most grateful!

05:57.510 --> 05:59.840
Well then, I'll contact them in short order.

05:59.840 --> 06:01.920
I think they'll be able to start posthaste.

06:01.920 --> 06:03.680
Lookin' forward to it.

06:03.680 --> 06:05.180
Now listen, you...

06:05.530 --> 06:09.140
What's the problem? I'm staying 
in Astarl for a while anyway.

06:09.140 --> 06:11.030
You are here on official business.

06:11.030 --> 06:14.580
As the first prince of Delbaran, 
you must conduct yourself appropriately.

06:14.580 --> 06:16.060
Yeah. Sure, sure.

06:16.360 --> 06:18.820
Your Majesty. Queen Laura.

06:18.820 --> 06:23.070
I simply cannot express how honored 
we are to have been invited here today.

06:23.070 --> 06:26.790
Such formality is unnecessary, Duke Dorman.

06:26.790 --> 06:29.900
After all, we shall soon be family.

06:29.900 --> 06:32.300
Oh, and what joy that brings me!

06:32.300 --> 06:34.160
Is this your girl?

06:34.160 --> 06:37.180
Yes. Come, Leticia.

06:39.670 --> 06:41.360
My!

06:39.670 --> 06:41.360
Oh!

06:43.500 --> 06:46.140
Leticia, come here, dear.

06:52.040 --> 06:53.580
Ah, Lettie!

06:53.580 --> 06:54.610
Oh...

06:55.270 --> 06:56.730
What is it?

06:56.730 --> 06:59.110
Gracious, how adorable!

07:00.600 --> 07:04.280
I've always wanted such a darling daughter.

07:08.000 --> 07:08.990
Huh?

07:19.180 --> 07:20.620
So, did you read that book?

07:20.620 --> 07:21.590
Huh?

07:22.000 --> 07:25.620
<i>The Sorrows of Young Gordon</i>.
The one everyone's talking about.

07:25.620 --> 07:28.590
Yeah, I read it. I didn't like the ending.

07:28.590 --> 07:30.870
That sounds just like you.

07:30.870 --> 07:34.140
I can understand why you'd want him to live,

07:34.140 --> 07:36.850
but I found it an interesting 
conclusion for a tragedy.

07:37.160 --> 07:39.450
I don't like sad love stories.

07:39.450 --> 07:42.610
The stuff poets write is usually tragic.

07:42.610 --> 07:45.920
I can understand why people 
like tragedies so much,

07:46.350 --> 07:49.110
but I'd rather spend my time 
on happier love stories.

07:53.260 --> 07:55.080
She's so cute.

07:55.080 --> 07:56.330
Prince Clarke.

07:58.760 --> 08:00.140
Prince Clarke?

08:00.140 --> 08:02.000
Whoa! Who are you?!

08:02.000 --> 08:05.030
Pardon me. Did I startle you?

08:05.030 --> 08:08.470
My name is Nadir Dorman. 
I am Leticia's older brother.

08:08.470 --> 08:09.920
So you're the one?

08:09.920 --> 08:13.970
The scoundrel who's trying to take advantage 
of our engagement for your own ends?

08:13.970 --> 08:16.930
Is that what the rumors say? 
That's unfortunate.

08:17.260 --> 08:21.940
I merely wish to make my little sister happy.

08:23.530 --> 08:26.440
Okay, Nadir. I'll remember that.

08:26.440 --> 08:29.370
Now, if I may ask, what are you 
doing outside this room?

08:29.370 --> 08:30.840
I'm not doing anything.

08:30.840 --> 08:31.680
Is that so?

08:31.680 --> 08:32.450
What?

08:32.450 --> 08:33.450
Oh, it's nothing.

08:38.910 --> 08:40.770
Do you require assistance?

08:40.770 --> 08:42.180
No, I'm fine.

08:42.180 --> 08:44.550
Are you on Clarke's side now, Uncle?

08:44.550 --> 08:48.880
Nathan, I certainly wouldn't take 
the side of anyone who calls me "Uncle."

08:53.390 --> 08:54.260
Oh?

08:57.430 --> 08:58.870
Checkmate.

09:03.130 --> 09:04.230
Ah...

09:04.510 --> 09:06.510
It looks like you should have moved left.

09:06.510 --> 09:08.340
How about it, Nadir? One game?

09:08.340 --> 09:09.980
I won't go easy on you.

09:09.980 --> 09:11.470
Nathan's quite good.

09:11.470 --> 09:12.990
Which color would you like?

09:13.350 --> 09:14.480
I'll take black.

09:16.850 --> 09:21.630
You know, your poker face isn't going 
to save you on the chessboard.

09:22.230 --> 09:25.130
The kindhearted cannot win at chess.

09:27.000 --> 09:31.450
The game of chess, like love or music, 
brings joy to people's hearts.

09:31.450 --> 09:36.010
It's certainly a lovely way to pass the time.
I wish you both a lovely game together.

09:36.010 --> 09:39.680
When you protect your pieces, 
they protect you in return.

09:39.680 --> 09:43.710
This may take a while. 
Let us send for some tea.

10:31.830 --> 10:33.050
Leticia.

10:35.460 --> 10:36.690
Let's go back.

10:36.690 --> 10:37.660
No!

10:37.660 --> 10:40.040
Everyone's worried. 
They're all looking for you.

10:44.240 --> 10:46.540
Leticia, are you in here?

10:47.850 --> 10:49.120
Brother?

10:54.080 --> 10:55.340
Brother!

10:56.950 --> 10:59.920
You really shouldn't run off like that.

10:59.920 --> 11:03.050
Those people scare me. I want to go home!

11:04.140 --> 11:06.040
I guess I can't blame you.

11:08.730 --> 11:12.940
Prince Clarke, I would like 
to take her home for the day.

11:13.330 --> 11:17.040
I will make sure she understands the gravity
of fulfilling her duties starting tomorrow.

11:17.390 --> 11:18.850
Please excuse us.

11:24.670 --> 11:25.960
Fine.

11:51.770 --> 11:53.730
Is this regarding Leticia?

11:54.210 --> 11:58.030
That's right. In the five years 
since she started princess lessons,

11:58.030 --> 12:00.650
she's become increasingly unhappy.

12:01.120 --> 12:03.640
She's stopped laughing in a crude fashion,

12:03.640 --> 12:06.000
and she's praised as the
 very picture of propriety.

12:06.000 --> 12:07.900
But that isn't good for her!

12:08.480 --> 12:10.500
I want Leticia to keep laughing.

12:10.500 --> 12:14.500
I see. So, what is your reason 
for summoning me?

12:14.500 --> 12:17.070
I want to ask someone 
who knows Leticia well...

12:17.070 --> 12:19.360
What do I have to do to make her smile?

12:19.360 --> 12:23.200
Well, let's see. Why not give her a gift?

12:23.200 --> 12:24.970
Of course! What would she like?

12:26.570 --> 12:27.980
Baked goods, perhaps.

12:29.180 --> 12:31.010
I brought you a present today.

12:34.120 --> 12:36.120
Thank you, Your Highness.

12:37.210 --> 12:38.390
Open it up.

12:39.680 --> 12:41.650
I ordered some delicious treats for you.

12:41.650 --> 12:43.250
How very exciting.

12:43.720 --> 12:44.620
You know...

12:44.620 --> 12:45.680
What is it?

12:48.010 --> 12:49.620
No, never mind.

12:50.330 --> 12:52.380
She didn't even open my present.

12:52.380 --> 12:54.630
I'm sure she enjoyed it in her room, though.

12:54.630 --> 12:55.690
Really?

12:57.420 --> 12:58.390
Yes.

12:58.390 --> 13:01.010
Then why does she always 
act so formal around me?

13:01.010 --> 13:03.080
Do you wish to be closer with her?

13:03.080 --> 13:04.340
I do.

13:04.340 --> 13:05.860
Well, let's see.

13:05.860 --> 13:10.860
The way she calls you "Highness" <i>does</i>
 suggest some distance between you.

13:10.860 --> 13:12.400
Yes, I can feel it.

13:12.950 --> 13:17.150
The first step to getting closer may be 
to call each other by name.

13:17.150 --> 13:18.670
Our names! That's it!

13:20.110 --> 13:22.860
Wait, why is it that you never 
address me formally?

13:22.860 --> 13:24.790
As you are my prospective brother-in-law,

13:24.790 --> 13:26.830
I'd like to stay on familiar terms.

13:27.140 --> 13:30.340
I'm not <i>your</i> prospective brother. 
You're <i>my</i> prospective brother.

13:30.780 --> 13:32.830
Either way is fine with me,

13:33.220 --> 13:36.110
but would you prefer that I address you 
as "Your Highness," then?

13:36.110 --> 13:38.850
Yeah, I would. 
You should call me "Your Highness."

13:38.850 --> 13:40.490
Very well, Prince Clarke.

13:41.610 --> 13:43.680
Leticia, look at these roses.

13:43.680 --> 13:45.160
Yes, Your Highness.

13:45.610 --> 13:48.240
The rose holds special meaning 
for the Kingdom of Astarl.

13:48.710 --> 13:52.440
They are cherished dearly as symbols 
of freedom and peace.

13:52.440 --> 13:53.440
Also...

13:54.440 --> 13:56.890
they're beautiful, just like you.

13:59.630 --> 14:00.540
Huh?

14:01.120 --> 14:02.280
Huh?

14:02.280 --> 14:04.200
If you say so, Your Highness.

14:04.200 --> 14:05.480
What?!

14:05.480 --> 14:07.380
Say, Leticia...

14:07.380 --> 14:08.660
What is it?

14:08.660 --> 14:13.410
We're going to be married. 
That means we'll be man and wife!

14:13.840 --> 14:17.210
And once we are, that will make us equals.

14:18.000 --> 14:20.810
That may be true for the average household,

14:20.810 --> 14:24.720
but don't you agree that the king and queen
are of very different stations, Your Highness?

14:25.010 --> 14:27.380
The king and queen are equals, too!

14:27.720 --> 14:32.080
So you don't have to address me formally.
You can just call me Clarke.

14:32.080 --> 14:35.400
I have learned that it is best to uphold 
proper decorum in such situations.

14:35.400 --> 14:38.480
so as to set a good example for 
nobility and commoners alike.

14:38.830 --> 14:41.670
Or... is that an order?

14:43.030 --> 14:44.390
No!

14:44.390 --> 14:45.950
It's just a personal request.

14:46.500 --> 14:47.790
I see.

14:48.930 --> 14:51.520
In that case, I shall 
call you "Prince Clarke"...

14:53.960 --> 14:56.210
after I confirm that it is permissible.

14:57.970 --> 14:58.980
Okay.

15:01.610 --> 15:02.970
So, what do you think?

15:02.970 --> 15:04.220
About what?

15:04.720 --> 15:07.410
I want to know how Leticia feels about me.

15:07.410 --> 15:09.300
This again?

15:09.300 --> 15:11.510
May I have permission to speak frankly?

15:11.510 --> 15:12.770
That's fine with me.

15:13.470 --> 15:16.270
She isn't the slightest bit interested in you.

15:18.500 --> 15:19.990
I knew it.

15:20.730 --> 15:23.910
She is, of course, aware
 she is engaged to the prince,

15:23.910 --> 15:26.750
but it is unclear whether 
she would even recognize you.

15:26.750 --> 15:28.450
Does she hate me?

15:28.450 --> 15:31.650
I doubt she has any feelings 
toward you whatsoever.

15:32.340 --> 15:35.380
Why doesn't she react at all 
when I talk to her?

15:35.870 --> 15:39.220
I expect she perceives your voice
as one would the chirping of a bird.

15:39.750 --> 15:40.910
Oh no!

15:40.910 --> 15:44.670
Well, at least she doesn't hate me. 
I should look on the bright side. Yeah.

15:44.670 --> 15:47.990
Birdsong is pleasant enough
 anyway, so I should be good.

15:47.990 --> 15:51.370
All I want is to secure a position 
close to the royal family.

15:51.370 --> 15:55.750
For now, my most direct route is to see
 that Leticia marries Prince Clarke.

15:55.750 --> 15:59.480
However, my sister and this prince 
are proving totally useless!

15:59.860 --> 16:01.430
What do you think I should do?

16:01.430 --> 16:05.380
I think your first priority should be 
to get Leticia to drop her mask.

16:05.380 --> 16:06.410
But how?

16:06.410 --> 16:08.560
Take a lover other than her.

16:08.560 --> 16:09.680
Absolutely not!

16:09.680 --> 16:11.160
You just have to pretend.

16:11.430 --> 16:13.720
If she sees you with another woman,

16:13.720 --> 16:17.330
she'll likely assume your engagement
 is off and show her true colors.

16:17.820 --> 16:18.800
I see!

16:18.800 --> 16:24.750
I expect she will confront you about it, 
but you absolutely, absolutely, <i>absolutely</i>

16:24.750 --> 16:27.840
must not state explicitly
 that the engagement is off.

16:28.880 --> 16:30.090
You really think it'll work?

16:30.090 --> 16:33.300
I know everything there is 
to know about her behavior.

16:33.300 --> 16:34.260
All right then.

16:34.550 --> 16:38.550
So feel free to be with whomever, 
sire as many offspring as you want,

16:38.550 --> 16:40.380
and bring prosperity to your kingdom!

16:40.380 --> 16:42.520
Now then, farewell!

16:44.800 --> 16:46.780
Dorman family carriage, come on!

16:55.510 --> 16:57.660
Didn't you tell me this was gonna work?

16:57.660 --> 16:59.360
This is only the beginning.

16:59.830 --> 17:01.790
Are you sure she didn't simply escape?

17:01.790 --> 17:06.760
Not now that she's finally acknowledged 
your existence as a human being.

17:06.760 --> 17:08.950
Our work is just starting.

17:08.950 --> 17:11.300
So what should we do next?

17:11.300 --> 17:15.260
For now, why don't we go 
to meet her in Aberta?

17:36.190 --> 17:39.080
She has such a pretty smile!

17:39.080 --> 17:41.360
Huh? Huh?

17:46.560 --> 17:48.590
What? Ah...

17:51.230 --> 17:51.970
Huh?

18:05.380 --> 18:08.320
Ah, oh, wh-wh-whoa!

18:31.670 --> 18:34.800
What in the world is this? 
What am I supposed to be watching here?

18:35.550 --> 18:36.700
I swear...

18:44.080 --> 18:45.030
Prince Clarke!

18:45.030 --> 18:45.980
Huh? Whoa!

18:46.320 --> 18:49.660
What do you think you're doing? 
Hurry up and go say something to her!

18:49.660 --> 18:50.480
Oh, that's right!

18:50.480 --> 18:52.060
Ah, Nadir.

18:52.060 --> 18:56.210
Arrange to have a stream dug in the courtyard
so it's possible to go fishing in the castle.

18:56.740 --> 18:57.820
What?

18:57.820 --> 18:58.970
Take care of it.

19:07.110 --> 19:08.410
Looks like you're having fun.

19:08.410 --> 19:10.190
Wuh? Whoa!

19:11.940 --> 19:13.820
Are you happy now?

19:13.820 --> 19:16.100
Is Leticia always like this?

19:16.100 --> 19:17.520
Yes, she is.

19:17.520 --> 19:18.760
No fair.

19:18.760 --> 19:19.670
What?

19:20.050 --> 19:24.400
You get to see her cute side all the 
time just because you're her brother.

19:25.110 --> 19:26.020
It's not fair.

19:26.020 --> 19:28.090
What are you talking about?

19:28.090 --> 19:29.950
We can still take her back, right?

19:30.310 --> 19:32.060
Of course we can.

19:32.390 --> 19:35.820
But why don't you take this 
opportunity to catch her yourself?

19:36.760 --> 19:37.970
Catch her?

19:38.360 --> 19:39.280
Yes.

19:39.920 --> 19:41.230
Are you okay?

19:42.660 --> 19:44.220
Prince Clarke?

19:45.230 --> 19:46.810
Hey, Lettie.

19:51.100 --> 19:52.970
Wow.

19:55.520 --> 19:56.880
Um...

19:57.380 --> 19:59.390
The doll is talking!

19:59.390 --> 20:03.240
Huh? I'm Clarke. I'm not a doll.

20:03.660 --> 20:06.610
Clarke... the prince?

20:07.620 --> 20:10.150
Hey, why don't we get out of here?

20:12.640 --> 20:13.900
Yeah!

20:28.180 --> 20:29.670
She's laughing.

20:30.090 --> 20:33.530
At the moment, it seems things 
are going more or less as I planned.

20:33.530 --> 20:35.040
That's not the issue.

20:35.040 --> 20:35.990
Huh?

20:35.990 --> 20:39.020
Well, yes, I suppose your plan is working.

20:39.020 --> 20:42.380
Arrange invitations 
for guests to mislead Leticia,

20:42.380 --> 20:45.520
arrange for an evening ball
but keep the details secret,

20:45.520 --> 20:48.180
arrange to have Leticia return to Aberta,

20:48.180 --> 20:50.220
plus submit to the prince's whims

20:50.220 --> 20:53.940
and arrange for a stream to be made 
for fishing in the castle garden.

20:53.940 --> 20:58.220
Considering everything I have done 
to try to keep my sister happy so far,

20:58.220 --> 21:01.010
there is no way she 
will not be getting married!

21:02.460 --> 21:03.700
I appreciate your help.

21:04.160 --> 21:09.210
I'll be satisfied once you and Leticia 
produce an heir together.

21:10.270 --> 21:12.330
Only if she says it's okay.

21:13.290 --> 21:14.290
Huh?

21:14.760 --> 21:17.550
Don't tell me you haven't even made a move yet!

21:18.250 --> 21:19.550
I haven't.

21:19.840 --> 21:21.190
You can't be serious!

21:21.190 --> 21:24.570
We aren't even married yet. 
Of course I haven't.

21:24.980 --> 21:28.930
You have your fiancée living with you in 
the castle and you haven't made a move?

21:28.930 --> 21:30.920
Not until we're married.

21:30.920 --> 21:33.580
And even then, 
I'll wait until Leticia says okay.

21:33.580 --> 21:35.300
Oh, I give up.

21:35.300 --> 21:40.280
It may be some years yet before 
you become the uncle to the future king.

21:40.280 --> 21:41.450
What's this now?

21:42.200 --> 21:44.750
Have you two been plotting something?

21:48.360 --> 21:49.950
Absolutely not!

23:19.920 --> 23:39.940
<b>Next Time</b>

23:20.040 --> 23:25.050
I'm going to be angry if you call me "Uncle"

23:20.920 --> 23:25.930
Ah... how regrettable

23:21.920 --> 23:26.930
I love to see her smiling

23:22.920 --> 23:27.930
How sad indeed...

23:23.920 --> 23:28.930
Leticia Dorman isn't the type to give up over simply being scolded

23:25.930 --> 23:30.930
What is this? What happened?!

23:27.300 --> 23:32.310
Bye-bye. Let's play again

23:28.800 --> 23:33.810
I've taken a liking to this place

23:30.300 --> 23:35.310
Um... would you mind at least sending it?

23:31.810 --> 23:36.810
Prince Clarke, what is that?

23:37.270 --> 23:39.940
Bonjour, les amants
